  "changelog": [
    "OptiScaler now comes from OptiScaler-FFXIV, the maintainer's own fork: its first release, 2026.10.19, built on upstream OptiScaler d9b62110 (tag ffxiv-2026.10.19-d9b62110).",
    "NVIDIA DLSS, frame generation and Neural Rendering are updated to 310.9.16, with Streamline 2.14.16.",
    "RTX 20, 30 and 40 now share one tier, RTX 20/30/40. RTX 50 gets its own tier, community-verified: its Neural Rendering runtime is NVIDIA's own file, and the maintainer cannot test it.",
    "Lucent no longer replaces the game's own nvngx_dlss.dll in the game folder, and drops the files OptiScaler-FFXIV doesn't use: the NVFP4 hybrid files, nvngx_dlssd.dll and the Streamline plugins it never loads.",
    "The OptiScaler menu has a new look: charcoal with the Crunchyroll orange accent, in Segoe UI. It applies to new installs and Reset; an existing OptiScaler.ini keeps its own colours.",
    "New installs and Reset also start with the fork's newer options on: HUD-less frame generation, window mode, automatic mipmap bias, nameplate interpolation and the character preview's Neural Rendering before DLSS. The game jitter correction and the HUD-less diagnostics are on as well; both are experimental or for diagnosis, and the log says what they do."
  ],
